wireguard: queueing: preserve tstamp_type when encapsulating packet

Mainline commit 65ab9de4bdd4 (Linux 7.3), applied to amneziawg's copy of queueing.h, which the
amneziawg tree does not carry yet. amneziawg keeps a compat branch around the headers memset,
so the hunk is adapted rather than applied verbatim.

skb_scrub_packet() keeps a monotonic skb->tstamp, but the headers memset clears
skb->tstamp_type, so the encapsulated packet carries a monotonic timestamp labelled realtime.
Since Linux 7.2 sch_fq checks the label and logs "fq: likely mono tstamp" for every such packet.

--- a/src/queueing.h
+++ b/src/queueing.h
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@
 	u8 l4_hash = skb->l4_hash;
 	u8 sw_hash = skb->sw_hash;
 	u32 hash = skb->hash;
+	u8 tstamp_type = skb->tstamp_type;
 	skb_scrub_packet(skb, true);
 #ifdef COMPAT_SKB_HAS_SKB_START
 	memset(&skb->headers_start, 0,
@@ -93,6 +94,7 @@
 		skb->l4_hash = l4_hash;
 		skb->sw_hash = sw_hash;
 		skb->hash = hash;
+		skb->tstamp_type = tstamp_type;
 	}
 	skb->queue_mapping = 0;
 	skb->nohdr = 0;
